ull}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's trip is booked and both reservations are confirmed. The combined booking didn't fully work, so the flight and hotel ended up as two separate reservations.\n\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, SFO to JFK, nonstop, 2026-11-12, $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. F120 was cheaper at $199, but it has a stop.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge, New York, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total. This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What happened with the combined booking:** My first combined booking attempt timed out. I retried with the same request ID, which can't create a duplicate booking. The system then said the original request had partly failed: the flight was booked, but the hotel step hit an internal error. The reservation list showed only the flight, so I booked the hotel by itself. A final check shows each item booked once and no duplicate charges.", "type": "text"}]}]}